# PromQL Query

Paste the following query exactly as shown.

```promql
avg(process_cpu_usage{job="auth-service"})
```

Click

```
Run Queries
```

Notice that this is exactly the same query used for the CPU Usage Gauge.

The only difference is the visualization.

---

# Understanding the Query

The metric

```promql
process_cpu_usage
```

is exposed by Micrometer.

It measures the percentage of CPU currently consumed by the Java process.

Using

```promql
avg(...)
```

produces the average CPU utilization across all running application Pods.

This ensures that the graph remains accurate as the application scales horizontally.

